Whisper: the Windows installer installs for the current user, without elevation

What: the installer's default folder is %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Whisper instead of
Program Files; it no longer asks for administrator rights up front (a folder the user
cannot write to still asks when it is picked); it registers Whisper for the current
user only (HKCU: Apps & Features, Start menu, file and protocol handlers), also when it
runs elevated. Apps & Features shows Whisper's own version and Whisper as the
publisher (Firefox writes "Mozilla" there). The uninstaller keeps the
profile unless the user says otherwise: it asks (No is the default) and, when silent,
deletes the profile only with /PURGE (which uninstall\helper.exe now hands on to the
uninstaller it starts; Firefox's passes only /S). The "reinstalled" marker that makes the browser
offer a profile reset is kept under Whisper's own registry key, not Firefox's, next to a
note of what the uninstaller did with the profile.
Why: a per-user install needs no administrator rights, and the updater can replace
its files without a UAC prompt or Mozilla's maintenance service (which Whisper does not
build). Firefox's uninstaller wrote that marker under Software\Mozilla\Firefox, so
uninstalling Whisper would have made Firefox offer to reset its profile, and Whisper
would have read and cleared Firefox's marker.
---
diff --git a/browser/components/ReinstallCheck.sys.mjs b/browser/components/ReinstallCheck.sys.mjs
index eb97d70db4..d687ce6700 100644
--- a/browser/components/ReinstallCheck.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/ReinstallCheck.sys.mjs
@@ -27,14 +27,16 @@ function readAndClearUninstalledValue() {
     ).UpdateUtils.UpdateChannel;
   } catch (ex) {}
   if (updateChannel) {
+    // Whisper: Whisper's uninstaller writes under Whisper's own key, so Firefox's
+    // marker is never read or cleared here.
     let uninstalledValue = lazy.WindowsRegistry.readRegKey(
       Ci.nsIWindowsRegKey.ROOT_KEY_CURRENT_USER,
-      "Software\\Mozilla\\Firefox",
+      `Software\\Whisper\\${AppConstants.MOZ_APP_BASENAME}`,
       `Uninstalled-${updateChannel}`
     );
     let removalSuccessful = lazy.WindowsRegistry.removeRegKey(
       Ci.nsIWindowsRegKey.ROOT_KEY_CURRENT_USER,
-      "Software\\Mozilla\\Firefox",
+      `Software\\Whisper\\${AppConstants.MOZ_APP_BASENAME}`,
       `Uninstalled-${updateChannel}`
     );
     return removalSuccessful && uninstalledValue == "True";
diff --git a/browser/installer/windows/nsis/installer.nsi b/browser/installer/windows/nsis/installer.nsi
index bdae08d333..c5990cca9b 100755
